  "title": "capture: Silence Coverity 1560008",
  "description": "GLib's manual says \"[a]s all GLib functions and data structures use\ng_malloc() internally, unless otherwise specified, any allocation\nfailure will result in the application being terminated.\" g_strdup()\nis such a function, so if it fails, the application will terminate.\nFor that reason, everywhere else we don't check for failure after\ng_strdup.\n\nError handling that tries to g_strdup another similar sized string\nalso probably wouldn't work anyway.\n\nFor some reason, Coverity worries about a leak in this path. Just\neliminate the error handling that doesn't actually handle anything.",
